      "writtenOn": "2026-07-31T19:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "http_ts_builtin_tx_callback is generated only when http ask for it. in case of http/1 and http/2 when we try send app data to underlying transport (tcp ot tls) and tx fifo is full, this happen when http has tx event from app (http/1 immediately from cutstom_tx callback or http/2 tx scheduler), in addition to asking tcp/tls for dequeue notification we deschedule app session so we don\u0027t receive new tx events from it. when http_ts_builtin_tx_callback is invoked we call transport_connection_reschedule which generate tx event for http and in next dispatch we enqueue new portion of data to tcp/tls tx fifo and update timer.\nwhat you described mean that http do not try to enqueue data, no tx event and timer update, after it get dequeue notification from tcp/tls. in my opinion updating timer in http_ts_builtin_tx_callback just help but don\u0027t fix real issue which is probably something completely different",
